<title>SWEDEN: ABB Power Systems wins 220 mln skr orders.</title>
<headline>ABB Power Systems wins 220 mln skr orders.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1996-09-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swiss-Swedish electrical engineering group Asea Brown Boveri AB said on Friday its ABB Power Systems division won contracts worth 220 million crowns.</p>
<p>&quot;ABB Power Systems has received orders for a number of plants for shunt and series compensation and improved power quality,&quot; ABB spokesman Hans-Ake Jonsson told Reuters.</p>
<p>One of the contracts would strengthen the electrical power transmission connection between Sweden and Finland. The others would improve power connections in tourist areas in North Carolina in the U.S. and Cancun in Mexico.</p>
<p>-- Abigail Schmelz, Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700-1003</p>
</text>
